Last Updated: 01 July 2026

Welcome to the website of CITIS Infotech LLP.

By accessing or using this website, our digital platforms, programmes or services, you agree to comply with these Terms and Conditions. If you do not agree with these Terms, please do not use the website or services.

1. About CITIS Infotech

CITIS Infotech LLP provides education, technology, training, skill development, institutional transformation, Artificial Intelligence, coding, STEM, science learning, vocational education, industry-integrated learning and related services.

Specific programmes may be delivered independently or in collaboration with educational institutions, universities, schools, technology partners, certification bodies and other authorised partners.

2. Website Content

The content on this website is provided for general information about CITIS Infotech, its services, programmes and offerings.

While we make reasonable efforts to keep information accurate and updated, CITIS Infotech does not guarantee that all information on the website will always be complete, current or error-free.

Programme structures, curriculum, duration, fees, eligibility, certification arrangements and delivery models may change from time to time.

3. Programme Enrolment

Registration or submission of an enquiry does not automatically guarantee admission, enrolment, certification or placement.

Enrolment may be subject to:

Eligibility criteria 

Availability of seats 

Completion of registration formalities 

Payment of applicable fees 

Approval by the relevant institution or programme authority 

Submission of required documents 

Additional terms may apply to specific programmes.

4. Fees and Payments

Programme fees, registration fees and other applicable charges will be communicated separately through the relevant programme, proposal, admission communication, invoice or payment platform.

Users are responsible for ensuring that accurate payment information is provided.

CITIS Infotech reserves the right to suspend access to services where applicable payments remain unpaid, overdue or disputed.

5. Intellectual Property

Unless otherwise stated, the content, curriculum, text, graphics, designs, logos, videos, learning materials, technology, software and other intellectual property available through CITIS Infotech are owned by or licensed to CITIS Infotech or the respective rights holders.

Users may not copy, reproduce, distribute, modify, sell, publish or commercially exploit such content without prior written permission.

The CITIS Infotech name and logo may not be used without prior written authorisation.

6. User Responsibilities

Users agree not to:

Use the website or platforms for unlawful purposes 

Attempt unauthorised access to systems or accounts 

Interfere with website or platform functionality 

Upload malicious software or harmful content 

Misrepresent their identity or affiliation 

Copy or distribute protected learning content without authorisation 

Misuse programme certificates or credentials 

Violate the rights of CITIS Infotech or third parties 

7. Third-Party Platforms and Partners

Certain programmes or services may involve third-party platforms, technology providers, universities, certification organisations or industry partners.

Such services may also be governed by separate terms and conditions. CITIS Infotech is not responsible for changes, interruptions or policies of independent third-party providers beyond its reasonable control.

8. Certification

Completion of a programme does not automatically guarantee certification unless the learner satisfies all applicable academic, attendance, assessment, examination, payment and institutional requirements.

Certification may be issued by CITIS Infotech, a partner institution or an authorised certification body, depending on the specific programme.

9. Internships and Placements

CITIS Infotech may provide internship, career-readiness, industry-connect and placement support services.

However, unless specifically agreed in writing, CITIS Infotech does not guarantee employment, internships, interviews, salary levels or placement outcomes.

Employment and internship decisions remain the responsibility of the relevant employer or organisation.

10. Limitation of Liability

To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, CITIS Infotech shall not be liable for indirect, incidental, consequential or special losses arising from the use of the website or services.

CITIS Infotech shall not be responsible for interruptions caused by internet failures, technical issues, force majeure events or circumstances beyond its reasonable control.

11. Suspension or Termination

CITIS Infotech may suspend or terminate access to services where a user:

Violates these Terms 

Provides false information 

Misuses the platform or learning materials 

Engages in unlawful or inappropriate conduct 

Fails to make required payments 

12. Changes to Services

CITIS Infotech may modify, improve, update, replace or discontinue any aspect of its website, programme or services when reasonably necessary.

Where a programme is operated in collaboration with another institution, changes may also arise due to academic, regulatory or institutional requirements.

13. Governing Law

These Terms and Conditions shall be governed by the laws of India.

Any disputes shall be subject to the jurisdiction of the competent courts at [Insert City / Jurisdiction], unless otherwise specified in a programme-specific agreement.

14. Contact

For questions regarding these Terms, contact:

